       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.    "READSER",  is initial.
       AUTHOR.        Isaac Garcia Peveri.
       REMARKS.       Written in AcuCobol 7.0.0
      ******************************************************************
      * This example shows how to get a value from Arduino sensor      *
      * by calling a Tcp Serial Driver written in VB.NET               *
      * (as is a TCP driver, I am using C$SOCKET routine)              *
      ******************************************************************
      *
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       77 KEY-PRESSED PIC X.
       77 SOCKET-HANDLE  USAGE HANDLE.
      *   Arguments decoded by ARDUINO
       77 CMD-ARGS       PIC X(1)       VALUE SPACES.
       77 W-MESSAGE      PIC X(1)       VALUE 'R'.
      *
      /
      *++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++*
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
            DISPLAY 'COBOL CLIENT STARTED...'

               CALL 'C$SOCKET'         USING 3
                                          64000
                                          "127.0.0.1"
                                    GIVING SOCKET-HANDLE

            PERFORM WORKING-CYCLE
            PERFORM thread ACCEPT-KEYPRESS

            STOP RUN
            .
      /
      *++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++*
       WORKING-CYCLE.
            PERFORM UNTIL KEY-PRESSED = 'X' OR 'x'
               CALL "C$SLEEP"       USING 0.1

               CALL 'C$SOCKET'      USING 6
                                    SOCKET-HANDLE
                                    CMD-ARGS
                                    1
               DISPLAY 'INPUT RECEIVED: ' CMD-ARGS AT 0202

               EVALUATE CMD-ARGS
                   WHEN 'A' MOVE 1 TO W-MESSAGE
                   WHEN 'B' MOVE 2 TO W-MESSAGE
                   WHEN 'C' MOVE 3 TO W-MESSAGE
                   WHEN 'D' MOVE 4 TO W-MESSAGE
                   WHEN 'E' MOVE 5 TO W-MESSAGE
                   WHEN 'F' MOVE 6 TO W-MESSAGE
                   WHEN 'G' MOVE 7 TO W-MESSAGE
                   WHEN 'H' MOVE 8 TO W-MESSAGE
                   WHEN 'I' MOVE 9 TO W-MESSAGE
               END-EVALUATE

               CALL 'C$SOCKET'   USING 5
                                 SOCKET-HANDLE
                                 W-MESSAGE
                                 1

               MOVE SPACES TO KEY-PRESSED, CMD-ARGS
               CALL "C$SLEEP"       USING 0.1
            END-PERFORM
            .
      /
      *++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++*
       ACCEPT-KEYPRESS.
            PERFORM UNTIL KEY-PRESSED = 'X' or 'x'
               CALL "C$SLEEP" USING 0.5
               ACCEPT KEY-PRESSED ON EXCEPTION CONTINUE END-ACCEPT
            END-PERFORM
            .